SUMMARY:Bear Pen Gap\; a Saunter.
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the Sloth Hike Team of WNC: “We wi
 ll get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike
  groups don’t !!\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bsh_8qxUfDY**\nI am 
 going to try to find the blueberry field of the Bear Pen Gap section of th
 e MST. A few ppl are welcome to join me.\nHike Distance: 3.0 mi (apprx) Ac
 cum ascent: 500 ft.\nElevation: 5\,500 ft\nPace: **1.5mph – because I’
 m an ol’ Codger.**\nDifficulty: Very Rocky w/ roots. Single track\; In &
  Out.\n**Masticating will be ‘in motion’.**\nDrive time: 35mi/1 hr 1-w
 ay\nReturn Not earlier than: : 2:30 pm **(=4.5 hrs)**\nCarpool contributio
 ns appreciated. $5.00 suggested\nWeather Check: Waynesville\, NC\n*https:/
 /www.mountain-forecast.com/peaks/Richland-Balsam/forecasts/1954*\nWeather 
 cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED A
 S DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 3.0 driver(s). (=12ppl)\nWe suggest o
 pen windows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judg
 e accordingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of others
 .\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes 
 into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessant prattlers will be
  assumed to be having an affair. Obstreperous raucous yawping is discourag
 ed. My attempts to quiet the prattlers has failed. This has become a ‘so
 cial networking’ event.\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event 
 is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs.
  Well trained dogs **(you don’t have to yell)** can be 'off-leash'. 'On 
 leash' while meeting others on the trail.. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. La
 rge dogs will drive themselves.\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes led b
 y ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have challenging surprises.\nWood elves are
  mischievous in the Summer\; Zip your backpacks tight.\nAll hikes are at y
 our own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipme
 nt.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is a volunteer and not a profes
 sional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this event
 . There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participa
 nt\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability
  the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and membe
 rs for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occu
 r while participating in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle d
 uring this trip. **Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules a
 nd regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)
 \, and not to become intentionally separated from the group.** The leader(
 s) also has the right to use any images collected on this trip for recordi
 ng on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.
 com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pics: https:/
 /www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
