SUMMARY:Green River Adventures Tubing Event 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the **Sloth Hike Team of WNC**: “W
 e will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ 
 hike groups don’t ***!!***\n***https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2v
 t4***\nWe are going tubing on the Green River\; Up to 12 ppl are welcome t
 o join me.\nFloat Distance: 4.5mile. Accum descent: all downstream\nCost: 
 $30 prepaid – online.\n**READ RSVP instructions carefully and follow ste
 ps EXACTLY..\;-)**\n**READ Description below….**\nDrive time: 0.5 hrs 1-
 way\n**Return Not earlier than: 3PM (3-4 hrs on the river)**\nCarpool cont
 ributions appreciated. $3.00 suggested\nWeather Check: Saluda\, NC\nWeathe
 r cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED
  AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nWe currently have 7 driver(s) (=20ppl)\n**RSVP Instr
 uctions:**\nFirst: RSVP on HFF MeetUp to attend this event. If we have at 
 least 8 sign up by August 2\, we can get a group discount.\nSecond: Watch 
 for notification on Monday morning\, August 3\, to go online to register a
 nd pay.\nWhen you register\, you will be able to choose the type of tube y
 ou want to use. (single standard\, ergonomic or double tubes)\nYou will ch
 oose the 4.5 mile option and then pay online ($30). The link for more info
 rmation about the experience and to register is:\nhttps://greenriveradvent
 ures.com/adventure/tube-green-river/\nLocation of start point: Riverside O
 utpost\, 5476 Green River Cove Rd\, Saluda\, NC 28773.\nWe suggest slightl
 y open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so j
 udge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of oth
 ers.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy sho
 es into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\n**THIS IS -NOT- A DOG-PA
 RTICIPANT EVENT.**\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the Curm
 udgeon’ tend to have challenging surprises.\nWater nymphs tickle\, try n
 ot to laugh too hard – they scare easily.\nPack a snack/lunch and drink 
 in waterproof bag to keep with you while tubing. We can leave keys at the 
 check-in site. If you bring your phone\, put it in a waterproof bag with a
  lariat. Wear water shoes that will stay secure on your feet! If water is 
 low\, we may be walking part of the river. Sunscreen (???)\n**Tube the Gre
 en River in single standard\, ergonomic or double tubes.** Green River Tub
 ing will handle the gear and logistics\, while you enjoy this mellow river
  with **occasional Class II rapids**. 4.5-mile option (3-4hrs). This trip 
 starts at the Riverside Outpost located at 5476 Green River Cove Rd\, Salu
 da. **Please note that river levels vary daily and are rain dependent. We
 ’re having fun no matter the conditions!**\nAll hikes are at your own ri
 sk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaive
 r: : The organizer of this event is a volunteer and not a professional gui
 de. The function of the organizer is only to organize this event. There ar
 e certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by si
 gning up to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability the leade
 r(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any
  accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur while pa
 rticipating in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle during this
  trip. **Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules and regulat
 ions concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not
  to become intentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s) also ha
 s the right to use any images collected on this trip for recording on webs
 ite photo collections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**be
 fore** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.
 com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
